From 58fb1e7876536fc63b9a98934cdb2c46b3c1e4b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:27:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] test: cover a P2MR input named by its previous
 transaction

Repeat the swapped control block case with the input saying what it spends
through the whole previous transaction instead of the output alone, and hand it
to a blank wallet holding nothing but the tree. Signing has to put each block
back under the leaf the output proves, and a finalizer with no wallet at all has
to complete it, which is what makes the recovered associations load bearing.

Combining is checked the same way round, since a spent output read out of a
previous transaction settles a disagreement just as well as one named directly.

Finally, two PSBTs that say nothing at all about what they spend: neither
reading of a shared control block can be checked, so the side merged into keeps
its own, and above all the block may not end up under both leaves, which would
write one key twice.
